How can I use Go code to generate a story that describes Alice's emotions as she's stuck in traffic trying to get to her parent's house for Thanksgiving? 
Here's a sample Go code that uses emotion recognition to generate descriptive phrases:
package main
import (
    "fmt"
    "github.com/IBM/go-sdk-core/v5/core"
    "github.com/watson-developer-cloud/go-sdk/emotionv1"
)
func main() {
    // Set up the Emotion Analyzer client
    authenticator := &core.IamAuthenticator{
        ApiKey: "<YOUR_API_KEY>",
    }
    service, serviceErr := emotionv1.NewEmotionV1(&emotionv1.EmotionV1Options{
        Authenticator: authenticator,
    })
    if serviceErr != nil {
        panic(serviceErr)
    }
    service.SetServiceURL("<YOUR_SERVICE_URL>")
    // Analyze Alice's emotions
    result, _, err := service.Analyze(
        &emotionv1.AnalyzeOptions{
            Text: core.StringPtr("Alice is feeling frustrated and anxious as she sits in her car, barely moving in the Thanksgiving traffic."),
        },
    )
    if err != nil {
        panic(err)
    }
    // Generate descriptive phrases based on the analyzed emotions
    if result.Document != nil && result.Document.Emotion != nil {
        emotions := result.Document.Emotion
        fmt.Printf("Alice is feeling %s and %s as she struggles to make it to her parent's house for Thanksgiving.", emotions.ToneNames[0], emotions.ToneNames[1])
    }
}
This code uses the Watson Emotion Analyzer API to analyze Alice's emotions based on a provided text, and generates descriptive phrases based on the analyzed emotions. By modifying the input text and the descriptive phrases, you can generate a full story that describes Alice's emotional journey through Thanksgiving traffic.

