The most efficient way to find the median of a dataset of 1000 numbers is to use an algorithm called "Divide and Conquer". Here is a pseudocode to find the median of a dataset of n numbers:

function findMedian( dataSet )
    if ( length(dataSet) == 1 )
        return dataSet[1]

    midPosition = ceil( length(dataSet)/2 )
    leftDataSet = dataSet[1:midPosition]
    rightDataSet = dataSet[midPosition+1:]

    leftMedian = findMedian( leftDataSet )
    rightMedian = findMedian( rightDataSet )

    if ( leftMedian > rightMedian )
        return findMedian( leftDataSet )
    else
        return findMedian( rightDataSet )
end

